## 5. Parameter Validation and Remaining Technical Challenges (Objective Risk Assessment)
While the theoretical framework demonstrates internal consistency, translation to clinical trial environments requires precise, empirical quantification of two core variables:

* Optimization of the Kinetic Window Between Mobilization and Lysis: The precise chronological delay between LSC reactivation/mobilization and the peak cytotoxic activity of the infused cellular payload must be modeled continuously. This is critical to mitigate the risk of transient tumor acceleration and manage potential Tumor Lysis Syndrome (TLS) without empirical over-dosing.
* Kinetics of Therapeutic Cell Clearance: Because the recipient's underlying immune system remains intact, the rate of cellular clearance following the cessation of transient selective immunosuppression must be precisely mapped. Maintaining cellular persistence long enough to eradicate Minimal Residual Disease (MRD) while allowing the host immune system to eventually purge the allogeneic payload requires meticulous clinical calibration.

